      },
      {
        "id": "call_judge",
        "x": 2000,
        "y": 620,
        "width": 400
      },
      {
        "id": "openai-compatible",
        "x": -900,
        "y": 180,
        "width": 400
      },
      {
        "id": "teacher-model",
        "x": -420,
        "y": 180,
        "width": 400
      },
      {
        "id": "note_1",
        "x": -900,
        "y": -300,
        "width": 420,
        "node_type": "markdown_note",
        "name": "note_1",
        "markdown": "### Tool-Call Traces\nBuild the `{user_request, tool_call}` rows that teach a model to call functions.\n\n**The flow**\n- `tool_schema` invents a typed OpenAI function schema for a domain\n- `user_request` writes a request that needs that tool, with the values inside it\n- `tool_call` emits one structured call\n- `call_judge` scores schema validity and grounding\n\n**Why generate the schema**\nOne schema per row teaches the model to read arbitrary tools instead of memorising a fixed set. Swap in your own schemas with a seed when you want coverage of a real API.",
        "note_color": "#E0F2FE",
        "note_opacity": "35"
      },
      {
        "id": "note_2",
        "x": -430,
        "y": -300,
        "width": 420,
        "node_type": "markdown_note",
        "name": "note_2",
        "markdown": "**Pick a model first**\n`teacher-model` has no model set. A strong instruction model produces far better `tool_call` rows, because the failure mode is subtly invalid JSON.\n\n**Train with the schema in the prompt**\nRender `tool_schema` into the system message and `tool_call` as the assistant turn. A row without its schema teaches the model nothing useful.",
        "note_color": "#E0F2FE",
        "note_opacity": "35"
      }
    ],
    "edges": [
      {
        "from": "openai-compatible",
        "to": "teacher-model",
        "type": "semantic",
        "source_handle": "semantic-out",
        "target_handle": "semantic-in"
      },
      {
        "from": "teacher-model",
        "to": "tool_schema",
        "type": "semantic",
        "source_handle": "semantic-out",
        "target_handle": "data-in"
      },
      {
        "from": "teacher-model",
        "to": "user_request",
        "type": "semantic",
        "source_handle": "semantic-out",
        "target_handle": "data-in"
      },
      {
        "from": "teacher-model",
        "to": "tool_call",
        "type": "semantic",
        "source_handle": "semantic-out",
        "target_handle": "data-in"
      },
      {
        "from": "teacher-model",
        "to": "call_judge",
        "type": "semantic",
        "source_handle": "semantic-out",
        "target_handle": "data-in"
      },
      {
